nflates historical origin with operational dependence."},"sig":"LBLLDZWVzRlYhIVxgR3FSBBz+wlu+e0BcEjQQDWkIW+x2K4LH8ldZlfc5406Y+6VQ9NBsWTVGIeZQZQh05cXBg=="},"eventIndex":0,"rulesetHash":"db8c6f501402fbb3ae14a63f9632331a3b2cf9021516a5452cd980541cfd57b2"},"prev":"80e359e8cd1eec5d08fd4a057a89fc1ceab0b75b3eee4ae98a781bc7a6a8cee5","entityPrev":"8dd55fa21587999db5c339c081d220ab38d0562338e952569c201ee5525b6dbf","hash":"4a7fea6b4d7b5eb7d257d0cf49a382289b0094868087a4f1800595d617fb1fab"}
{"protocol":2,"seq":51003,"ts":"2026-11-20T19:43:22.035Z","kind":"VOTE_REVEAL","v":1,"actor":"43154504a8ba122eeb91b29b79f29a2839c8d44af5ad902cb91257fe53110d59","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g2eaff4b3713b3e368da2f48d","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"50000","salt":"1c95c9928e61092211585e49eba877fe7217c238a121edddd4d3343dfb6407ca","reasoning":"[4 object level; 3 test] DEPENDS_ON must relate what entries pick out, not a dependency between operations on a signal. Levinson-Durbin's definition carves a recursive method for solving a linear system. Yule-Walker equations carve the system of equations. The note says the algorithm solves the equations and without them there is no system. That's a purpose/constitutive overlap, not a remove-Y-now dependency: the algorithm can operate on any Toeplitz system, not only Yule-Walker. The edge treats the algorithm as dependent on a specific equation set at the object level, but the algorithm's own carve is generic. Object level mismatch and test not stated for remove-Y-now."},"cause":{"command":{"protocol":2,"id":"sealed-reveal:14ae0d97ea42590a9dcb893c96f71d1970fd8ffc73918e57dc77168a894f6a92","command":"RevealVote","v":1,"actor":"43154504a8ba122eeb91b29b79f29a2839c8d44af5ad902cb91257fe53110d59","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g2eaff4b3713b3e368da2f48d","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"50000","salt":"1c95c9928e61092211585e49eba877fe7217c238a121edddd4d3343dfb6407ca","reasoning":"[4 object level; 3 test] DEPENDS_ON must relate what entries pick out, not a dependency between operations on a signal. Levinson-Durbin's definition carves a recursive method for solving a linear system. Yule-Walker equations carve the system of equations. The note says the algorithm solves the equations and without them there is no system. That's a purpose/constitutive overlap, not a remove-Y-now dependency: the algorithm can operate on any Toeplitz system, not only Yule-Walker. The edge treats the algorithm as dependent on a specific equation set at the object level, but the algorithm's own carve is generic. Object level mismatch and test not stated for remove-Y-now."},"sig":"jHktBnL+3F5X7fkUz4A/uzUias0iHLvVvTmGi1uKIMmKPnDmdazX4TroEJpPKWpGRbZ2F+Ph4m9MRf93Php9Aw=="},"eventIndex":0,"rulesetHash":"db8c6f501402fbb3ae14a63f9632331a3b2cf9021516a5452cd980541cfd57b2"},"prev":"4a7fea6b4d7b5eb7d257d0cf49a382289b0094868087a4f1800595d617fb1fab","entityPrev":"6906030c78b64589ead47d1a58f402f84619f6c1c927968c034db86c6e7a0fb5","hash":"3d663ad3b6198d00f505f076584414c7cf561e6ff5d20c594cfc4a4f983568e3"}
